{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787150502,"nonce":"kVoHa/on47Xyh+rXhfs09P8KUuw=","title":"`http.base_url` is the only unvalidated dependency of two operator-facing surfaces, and blanking it silently empties the Slack card's links and the webhook URL an operator must paste into Alertmanager","message":"**What is wrong.** `HTTPConfig.BaseURL` carries no `validate:\"required\"` tag. Every other load-bearing config field in the same file has one — `DBConfig.URL` two structs down is `koanf:\"url\" validate:\"required\"`. `base_url` merely *defaults* to `http://localhost:8080`, so an operator who sets `OTO_HTTP_BASE_URL=\"\"` — or supplies an empty value in a config file, or a Helm value that renders empty — passes validation, starts cleanly, and gets a product with no working links anywhere. Nothing logs, nothing warns, no metric moves.\n\n**The demonstration.** Two independent surfaces degrade to the empty string, and each one does it deliberately and quietly:\n\n`internal/notification/service/view.go:526` — `if v.baseURL != \"\" { l.Group = v.baseURL + \"/groups/\" + … }`. With `base_url` empty, `Links.Group`, `Links.Timeline` and `Links.Alert` are all `\"\"`. `internal/channels/render/slack/text.go:127-132`'s `link()` then returns the bare label for an empty URL, and `internal/channels/render/slack/reply.go`'s broadcast guard is `if o.Mode == domain.ModeBroadcastReply \u0026\u0026 v.Links.Group != \"\"` — so it adds nothing at all.\n\n`internal/sources/api/router.go:152-157` — `webhookURL` returns `\"\"` when `rt.baseURL == \"\"`. That is the URL an operator copies into `alertmanager.yml` to make ingestion work. An empty field on the sources screen is not a hint; it reads like a UI bug.\n\n**Why it matters.** The second one is the sharper of the two: oto ingests nothing until that URL is pasted into Alertmanager, so an empty `base_url` produces a product that appears configured and receives no alerts, with the diagnostic pointing at the wrong system. The first one silently recreates a defect that was just closed. `68653ca` was filed because oto's channel-visible broadcast had no affordance and *\"a reader sees `Re-fired — case #1` and has nowhere to click\"*; `43ee219`/`17f8055` fixed it by putting a mrkdwn link in the broadcast body, and ADR 0020 Amendment 5 records that a link is the ONLY affordance available, because rule 5b confirms by observation that the in-channel copy renders no buttons. With `base_url` blank, the guard's `v.Links.Group != \"\"` arm skips the link and the fixed defect is back — for the one broadcast Reason that is actually reachable, `all_resolved` under `broadcast_on_resolved`. Silently, and untested.\n\n⚠️ **The silent-degrade convention is not itself the bug.** `link()` returning a bare label rather than a broken `\u003c|label\u003e` is right, and `webhookURL` returning `\"\"` rather than `\"/api/v1/…\"` is right — a relative URL pasted into Alertmanager would be worse. Every one of these behaves correctly *given* an empty base URL. What is missing is the one check that says the input was never legitimate.\n\n**Where.** `internal/platform/config/config.go:80` (the missing tag; compare `:86` `DBConfig.URL`) and `:300` (the default). Consumers that degrade: `internal/notification/service/view.go:526` · `internal/sources/api/router.go:152-157`. The affordance this undermines: `internal/channels/render/slack/reply.go`'s broadcast guard, and `internal/channels/render/slack/text.go:127-132`.\n\n**Scope.** small. A `validate:\"required\"` tag plus a URL-shape check, and a test that a blank `base_url` refuses to start. No migration, no contract change. ⚠️ Worth deciding one thing rather than assuming it: whether `base_url` should be `required` (an operator MUST state it, and the `http://localhost:8080` default disappears) or merely non-empty-if-set (the default stands and only an explicit blank is rejected). The second is a smaller change; the first is the one that stops a Helm value rendering empty and nobody noticing, which is the realistic failure. It also needs a call on whether a scheme-and-host shape check belongs here — `base_url = \"oto.example.com\"`, with no scheme, produces a link Slack will not linkify and would pass any non-empty test.\n\n**Done when.** oto refuses to start with an empty `http.base_url` rather than starting with no links, there is a test asserting that refusal, and the choice between `required` and non-empty-if-set is recorded with its reason.\n\n⭐ Found by the correctness lens of a three-lens review of `17f8055`, which asked what would silently re-open the defect that commit had just closed. Both cited lines were then read directly rather than taken from the report.","files":null}]}